{"doc_id": "doc16510", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The phrase \"the shot heard round the world\" refers to the beginning of the American Revolutionary War. While the conflict started with shots fired at Lexington, Massachusetts, pinpointing a single definitive first shot is historically difficult. Accounts of the initial exchanges there are often confused and some consider the event primarily a massacre rather than the first organized battle. However, it is established that the first shots fired by organized American forces occurred during the North Bridge skirmish, specifically when American militiamen fired their first volley while acting under specific orders.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1948760350, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "caf5cc53332965f43728e9b269b0429cc93475768f7f233a5f3c00cd8f097bb6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Americans acting under orders", "matched_aliases": ["Americans acting under orders"], "query_id": "test443", "question_hash": "72d8372bd8761dcdf3c20f18961ab9c263ac1cbaa3a9a95bf1b060a964f0d2a3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "55bbe4a9f74bc624ec1c79ec4beb8db6966101d0b2d095381bf9de61664c23ba", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 906460343, "similarity": 0.13632119514472454, "source_content_hash": "d6ddbb333191bbf14279ac7fd0e14a7dc97d649245312c482d2b470c0232f9c1", "source_hash": "2f75d7dcc9d4744746ac866f10f47ae42f5b3a7eea0d763d59249798ba958a66", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "dfaa9ee00b48aec11defb3e26c96373b74b527365bd19b9232fcd1cc10c2c8f4", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_